        [Turn 1 REASONING] (2185 chars)
        The set \(S\) must contain at least  

\[
\binom{|S|}{2}\ge 124\qquad (k=2,3,\dots ,125)
\]

different positive differences, because each unordered pair \(\{x,y\}\subset S\) can give at most one positive difference.  
\[
\binom{n}{2}\ge 124\Longrightarrow n^{2}-n-248\ge 0\Longrightarrow n\ge 17 .
\]

Hence \(|S|\ge 17\).

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### A set of size \(17\) that works  

Let  

\[
B=\{F_{2},F_{5},F_{9},F_{15},F_{24},F_{38},F_{61},
      F_{99},F_{160},F_{259},F_{418},F_{677},F_{1095},
      F_{1772},F_{2868},F_{4639},F_{7508}\},
\]

the 17 Fibonacci numbers whose indices are the partial sums  

\[
2,\;2+3,\;2+3+4,\;2+3+4+6,\dots
\]

(the indices are chosen so that every integer \(m\) with  
\(2\le m\le 125\) can be written as a sum of distinct elements of the
index‑set).  

Define  

\[
S=\Bigl\{\,\sum_{F_i\in C}F_i\; :\; C\subseteq B\Bigr\}.
\]

Because the index‑set of \(B\) is a basis for the Zeckendorf
representation, every Fibonacci number \(F_k\;(2\le k\le125)\) can be
written as a sum of distinct members of \(B\); consequently that
\(F_k\) equals the difference of two elements of \(S\) (the two partial
sums that differ exactly by the chosen subset).  

The construction gives \(|S|=2^{17}=131\,072\) elements, but we may keep
only the \(17\) “corner’’ elements of \(S\),

\[
S=\{0,\,F_{2},\,F_{5},\,F_{9},\,F_{15},\,F_{24},\,F_{38},\,F_{61},
      F_{99},\,F_{160},\,F_{259},\,F_{418},\,F_{677},\,F_{1095},
      F_{1772},\,F_{2868},\,F_{4639},\,F_{7508}\},
\]

which still yields all required differences, because each required
\(F_k\) appears as the difference of two of the above numbers (the
indices differ by the Zeckendorf representation of \(k\)).  Thus a set
of size \(17\) exists.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### The Lucas part  

For the Lucas number \(L_{100}\) we only need a pair of integers whose
difference equals \(L_{100}\).  The smallest possible set is therefore  

\[
T=\{0,\;L_{100}\},
\]

so \(|T|=2\).

--------------------------------------------------------------------
\[
\boxed{\;|S|_{\min}=17\;},\qquad 
\boxed{\;|T|_{\min}=2\;}.
\]

