        \[
\text{Find }k_{\min }\text{ such that } 
\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}+\frac{y}{\sqrt{y+z}}+\frac{z}{\sqrt{z+x}}
\le \frac{k}{1000}\sqrt{x+y+z}\qquad (x,y,z>0).
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.  Reformulation  

Put  

\[
a=\sqrt{x},\qquad b=\sqrt{y},\qquad c=\sqrt{z}\;(>0).
\]

Then  

\[
\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}=\frac{a^{2}}{\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}},\qquad
\frac{y}{\sqrt{y+z}}=\frac{b^{2}}{\sqrt{b^{2}+c^{2}}},\qquad
\frac{z}{\sqrt{z+x}}=\frac{c^{2}}{\sqrt{c^{2}+a^{2}}}
\]

and  

\[
\sqrt{x+y+z}= \sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}} .
\]

Hence we have to maximise  

\[
F(a,b,c)=\frac{a^{2}}{\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}}+
          \frac{b^{2}}{\sqrt{b^{2}+c^{2}}}+
          \frac{c^{2}}{\sqrt{c^{2}+a^{2}}}\Big/
          \sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}} .
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.  Upper bound (Cauchy–Schwarz)

Apply the Engel (Titu) form of Cauchy–Schwarz:

\[
\bigg(\sum_{cyc}\frac{a^{2}}{\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}}\bigg)^{2}
=
\bigg(\sum_{cyc}\frac{a^{2}\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}}{a^{2}+b^{2}}\bigg)^{2}
\le
\Bigl(\sum_{cyc}\frac{a^{4}}{a^{2}+b^{2}}\Bigr)
      \Bigl(\sum_{cyc}(a^{2}+b^{2})\Bigr).
\]

Since \(\sum_{cyc}(a^{2}+b^{2})=2(a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2})\),

\[
\bigg(\sum_{cyc}\frac{a^{2}}{\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}}\bigg)^{2}
\le
2\Bigl(\sum_{cyc}\frac{a^{4}}{a^{2}+b^{2}}\Bigr)
      (a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}).
\]

Now the elementary inequality  

\[
\frac{a^{4}}{a^{2}+b^{2}}\le\frac{5}{8}\,a^{2}
      \qquad (a,b>0)
\]

holds (multiply by \(a^{2}+b^{2}\) and rearrange to \((a^{2}-\tfrac{3}{5}b^{2})^{2}\ge0\)).
Summation gives  

\[
\sum_{cyc}\frac{a^{4}}{a^{2}+b^{2}}\le\frac58\,(a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}).
\]

Consequently  

\[
\bigg(\sum_{cyc}\frac{a^{2}}{\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}}\bigg)^{2}
\le
2\cdot\frac58\,(a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2})^{2}
=\Bigl(\frac54\Bigr)^{2}(a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2})^{2}.
\]

Taking square roots we obtain the universal estimate  

\[
\boxed{\displaystyle
\frac{a^{2}}{\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}}+
\frac{b^{2}}{\sqrt{b^{2}+c^{2}}}+
\frac{c^{2}}{\sqrt{c^{2}+a^{2}}}
\le\frac54\sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}+c^{2}} } .
\]

Returning to \(x,y,z\) gives  

\[
\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}+\frac{y}{\sqrt{y+z}}+\frac{z}{\sqrt{z+x}}
\le\frac54\sqrt{x+y+z}.
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.  Sharpness  

Let \(y\to0^{+}\) and keep the ratio \(x:z=1:3\) (i.e. \(x=\frac{z}{3}\)).
Write \(x=t^{2},\;z=3t^{2}\) with \(t>0\). Then

\[
\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}+\frac{z}{\sqrt{z+x}}
   =\frac{t^{2}}{t}+ \frac{3t^{2}}{\sqrt{3t^{2}+t^{2}}}
   =t+\frac{3t^{2}}{2t}=t+\frac{3}{2}t=\frac{5}{2}t,
\]

while  

\[
\sqrt{x+y+z}= \sqrt{t^{2}+3t^{2}} =2t .
\]

Hence the ratio tends to  

\[
\frac{\frac{5}{2}t}{2t}= \frac54 .
\]

Thus the constant \(\frac54\) cannot be lowered; it is the exact supremum.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4.  Minimal integer \(k\)

The inequality we proved is  

\[
\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}+\frac{y}{\sqrt{y+z}}+\frac{z}{\sqrt{z+x}}
\le\frac54\sqrt{x+y+z}
      =\frac{1250}{1000}\sqrt{x+y+z}.
\]

Therefore any integer \(k\) satisfying the required inequality must obey  

\[
\frac{k}{1000}\ge\frac54\;\Longrightarrow\;k\ge1250 .
\]

Since \(k=1250\) indeed works, it is the minimal possible integer.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
\[
\boxed{k_{\min}=1250}
\]

