        \[
\text{Find }k_{\min}\text{ such that } 
\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}+\frac{y}{\sqrt{y+z}}+\frac{z}{\sqrt{z+x}}
\le \frac{k}{1000}\sqrt{x+y+z}\qquad(\forall x,y,z>0).
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.  Reduce the problem to a maximisation

Define  

\[
R(x,y,z)=\frac{\displaystyle 
\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}+\frac{y}{\sqrt{y+z}}+\frac{z}{\sqrt{z+x}}}
{\sqrt{x+y+z}} .
\]

The required constant is  

\[
k_{\min}= \Bigl\lceil 1000\;\sup_{x,y,z>0} R(x,y,z)\Bigr\rceil .
\]

Because the inequality is homogeneous of degree \(0\) (both sides are
\(\sqrt{\text{length}}\)‑scaled), we may impose the normalisation  

\[
x+y+z=1 .
\]

Hence we have to maximise  

\[
F(x,y,z)=\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}+\frac{y}{\sqrt{y+z}}+\frac{z}{\sqrt{z+x}}
\qquad (x,y,z>0,\;x+y+z=1).
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.  Interior critical point

Using Lagrange multipliers for the interior (\(x,y,z>0\)) we obtain  

\[
\frac{\partial}{\partial x}\Bigl(F-\lambda(x+y+z)\Bigr)=0,
\quad\text{etc.}
\]

The system is symmetric, and its only interior solution is  

\[
x=y=z=\frac13 .
\]

For this point  

\[
F\Bigl(\tfrac13,\tfrac13,\tfrac13\Bigr)=\frac{3}{\sqrt6}
\approx1.2247 .
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.  Boundary case – one variable tends to \(0\)

Assume \(z\to0^{+}\).  
Then  

\[
F(x,y,0)=\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}+\sqrt{y},
\qquad
\sqrt{x+y+0}= \sqrt{x+y}.
\]

Hence  

\[
R(x,y,0)=\frac{x}{x+y}+\sqrt{\frac{y}{x+y}}
          =1-t+\sqrt{t},
\quad\text{where }t=\frac{y}{x+y}\in(0,1).
\]

The function \(g(t)=1-t+\sqrt t\) satisfies  

\[
g'(t)=-1+\frac{1}{2\sqrt t}=0\Longrightarrow \sqrt t=\frac12
\Longrightarrow t=\frac14 .
\]

Thus the maximum on the boundary is  

\[
g\!\left(\frac14\right)=1-\frac14+\frac12=\frac54=1.25 .
\]

It is approached when \(z\to0\) and \(y:x=1:3\) (i.e. \(x=3a,\;y=a\)).

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4.  Global maximum

The interior value \(3/\sqrt6\approx1.2247\) is smaller than the
boundary value \(5/4\).  
Since the function is continuous on the compact set
\(\{(x,y,z)\ge0,\;x+y+z=1\}\) and the only possible larger values lie on
the boundary, the global supremum is

\[
\sup_{x,y,z>0} R(x,y,z)=\frac54 .
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5.  Determination of \(k\)

Therefore  

\[
\frac{x}{\sqrt{x+y}}+\frac{y}{\sqrt{y+z}}+\frac{z}{\sqrt{z+x}}
\le \frac54\sqrt{x+y+z}\qquad(\forall x,y,z>0).
\]

The required constant is the smallest integer \(k\) with  

\[
\frac{k}{1000}\ge\frac54\;\Longrightarrow\;
k\ge 1000\cdot\frac54 =1250 .
\]

Hence  

\[
\boxed{k_{\min}=1250}.
\]

