Indeed, substituting \(Q(x)=c(x+2)(x-1)^{2}(x-4)\) gives  

\[
(x^{2}+x-2)Q(x-3)=(x+2)(x-1)\,c\,(x-1)(x-4)(x-7)
= c\,(x+2)(x-1)^{2}(x-4)(x-7)
\]

and  

\[
(x^{2}-11x+28)Q(x)=(x-4)(x-7)\,c\,(x+2)(x-1)^{2}(x-4)
= c\,(x+2)(x-1)^{2}(x-4)(x-7),
\]

so the two sides are identical for all \(x\).  
The zero polynomial (\(c=0\)) is also included.

