with a polynomial \(R(x)\). Substituting this into (1) and cancelling the common
factors \((x-4)(x-1)(x+2)\) (which are never zero simultaneously) gives  

\[
(x-1)R(x-3)=(x-7)R(x). \tag{2}
\]

