&\text{root }-2\;(k=-1) \text{ with multiplicity }1,\\
&\text{root } 1\;(k=0) \text{ with multiplicity }2,\\
&\text{root } 4\;(k=1) \text{ with multiplicity }1,
\end{aligned}
\]
and no other roots.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.  Form of \(Q\)

Hence, up to a constant factor \(c\in\mathbb C\),

\[
\boxed{\,Q(x)=c\,(x+2)(x-1)^{2}(x-4)\, } .
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4.  Verification

A direct substitution shows

\[
(x^{2}+x-2)Q(x-3)=(x^{2}-11x+28)Q(x)
\]

holds identically for any constant \(c\).  

Thus the set of all complex‑coefficient polynomials satisfying the given functional equation is exactly the one‑parameter family above.

