(x^{2}+x-2)Q(x-3)=(x^{2}-11x+28)Q(x)\qquad(\forall x\in\mathbb R)
\]

Factor the quadratics  

\[
x^{2}+x-2=(x+2)(x-1),\qquad 
x^{2}-11x+28=(x-4)(x-7),
\]

so the functional equation becomes  

\[
(x+2)(x-1)\,Q(x-3)=(x-4)(x-7)\,Q(x).\tag{1}
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.  Possible zeros of \(Q\)

Let \(a\) be a zero of \(Q\) (\(Q(a)=0\)).  
Putting \(x=a\) in (1) gives  

\[
(a+2)(a-1)\,Q(a-3)=0 .
\]

Hence, if \(a\neq-2,1\) then \(a-3\) is also a zero.  
Similarly, putting \(x=b+3\) with \(Q(b)=0\) yields  

\[
(b+5)(b+2)\,0=(b-1)(b-4)Q(b+3),
\]

so if \(b\neq1,4\) then \(b+3\) is a zero.  

Thus any zero different from \(-2,1,4\) would generate an infinite
arithmetic progression of zeros (step \(3\)), impossible for a
polynomial. Consequently every zero must belong to the set  

\[
\{-2,1,4\},
\]

and the set of zeros must be closed under the implications  

\[
-2\Rightarrow 1,\qquad 4\Rightarrow 1 .
\]

Hence the possible zero‑sets are  

\[
\varnothing,\; \{1\},\; \{-2,1\},\; \{1,4\},\; \{-2,1,4\}.
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.  Form of \(Q\)

Write \(Q\) with undetermined multiplicities:

\[
Q(x)=C\,(x-1)^{a}(x+2)^{b}(x-4)^{c},\qquad C\in\mathbb C,\;a,b,c\ge0 .
\]

Insert this into (1).  
Since  

\[
Q(x-3)=C\,(x-4)^{a}(x-1)^{b}(x-7)^{c},
\]

equation (1) becomes  

\[
(x+2)(x-1)^{b+1}(x-4)^{a}(x-7)^{c}
   =(x-4)^{c+1}(x-7)(x-1)^{a}(x+2)^{b}.
\]

Cancelling the non‑zero constant \(C\) and collecting powers of the
four distinct linear factors gives the exponent equalities  

\[
\begin{cases}
1-b = 0,\\[2pt]
b+1-a = 0,\\[2pt]
a-(c+1)=0,\\[2pt]
c-1 = 0 .
\end{cases}
\]

Solving yields  

\[
b=1,\qquad a=2,\qquad c=1 .
\]

Thus every non‑zero solution has the shape  

\[
Q(x)=C\,(x-1)^{2}(x+2)(x-4),\qquad C\in\mathbb C\setminus\{0\}.
\]

The zero polynomial also satisfies (1), so we may allow \(C=0\).

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.  Answer

All complex‑coefficient polynomials satisfying the given functional
equation are  

\[
\boxed{\,Q(x)=k\,(x-1)^{2}(x+2)(x-4)\quad\text{with }k\in\mathbb C\,}.
\]

(The choice \(k=0\) gives the zero polynomial.)

