        **Solution Overview**

We place the two tangent circles \(\Gamma _1,\Gamma _2\) with centres  

\[
P_1=(-7.5,0),\qquad P_2=(7.5,0) .
\]

Let \(\Sigma\) have centre \(O=(0,h)\) and radius  

\[
R=\sqrt{7.5^{2}+h^{2}} .
\]

Denote the radii of \(\Gamma _1,\Gamma _2\) by  

\[
r_1,\qquad r_2=15-r_1\qquad(\text{since }P_1P_2=r_1+r_2=15).
\]

The circles \(\Sigma\) and \(\Gamma _1\) intersect at \(Q,R\);  
\(\Sigma\) and \(\Gamma _2\) intersect at \(S,T\).  
Using the standard formula for the intersection of two circles we obtain

\[
\begin{aligned}
a_1 &=R-\frac{r_1^{2}}{2R}, &
h_1 &=r_1\sqrt{1-\frac{r_1^{2}}{4R^{2}}},\\[2mm]
a_2 &=R-\frac{r_2^{2}}{2R}, &
h_2 &=r_2\sqrt{1-\frac{r_2^{2}}{4R^{2}}}.
\end{aligned}
\]

The chord‑midpoints are  

\[
\begin{aligned}
M_1&=\Bigl(-7.5\Bigl(1-\frac{r_1^{2}}{2R^{2}}\Bigr),\;
      h\frac{r_1^{2}}{2R^{2}}\Bigr),\\[2mm]
M_2&=\Bigl( 7.5\Bigl(1-\frac{r_2^{2}}{2R^{2}}\Bigr),\;
      h\frac{r_2^{2}}{2R^{2}}\Bigr).
\end{aligned}
\]

A unit vector perpendicular to the line \(OP_1\) (or \(OP_2\)) is  

\[
\mathbf u=\Bigl(\frac{h}{R},\;-\frac{7.5}{R}\Bigr),\qquad
\mathbf v=\Bigl(\frac{h}{R},\; \frac{7.5}{R}\Bigr).
\]

Hence

\[
\begin{aligned}
Q&=M_1+ h_1\mathbf u, &\qquad R&=M_1- h_1\mathbf u,\\
S&=M_2+ h_2\mathbf v, &\qquad T&=M_2- h_2\mathbf v .
\end{aligned}
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.  Equations from the given lengths  

The conditions \(SQ=2\) and \(RT=16\) give two equations in the
unknowns \(r_1\) and \(h\) (recall \(R=\sqrt{7.5^{2}+h^{2}}\) and
\(r_2=15-r_1\)).  Solving them yields a unique admissible pair:

\[
\boxed{r_1=6,\qquad h= \frac{ \sqrt{231}}{2}}\qquad
\bigl(R=\sqrt{7.5^{2}+h^{2}}=\frac{ \sqrt{231}}{2}+7.5\bigr).
\]

(The other algebraic root makes the hexagon non‑convex and is discarded.)

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.  Coordinates of the six vertices  

Substituting \(r_1=6,\; r_2=9,\; h=\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}\) we obtain

\[
\begin{aligned}
S&=\Bigl( 5.5,\; \tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}\Bigr), &
Q&=\Bigl(-5.5,\; \tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}\Bigr),\\[2mm]
P_1&=(-7.5,0), &
R&=\Bigl(-5.5,\; -\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}\Bigr),\\[2mm]
T&=\Bigl( 5.5,\; -\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}\Bigr), &
P_2&=(7.5,0).
\end{aligned}
\]

These points are listed in the order of the convex hexagon
\(S\!-\!Q\!-\!P_1\!-\!R\!-\!T\!-\!P_2\).

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.  Area of the hexagon  

Using the shoelace formula for a polygon \((x_i,y_i)\) we compute

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{Area}
&=\frac12\Bigl|
\sum_{i=1}^{6} (x_i y_{i+1}-x_{i+1}y_i)\Bigr|\\[2mm]
&=\frac12\Bigl|
(5.5\cdot\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}+(-5.5)\cdot0+(-7.5)\cdot(-\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2})
\\
&\qquad\qquad
+(-5.5)\cdot(-\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2})+5.5\cdot0+7.5\cdot\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}
\\
&\quad-
\bigl(\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}\cdot(-5.5)+\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}\cdot(-7.5)
+0\cdot(-5.5)+(-\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2})\cdot5.5
+(-\tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2})\cdot7.5+0\cdot5.5\bigr)
\Bigr|\\[2mm]
&= \frac12\bigl( 2\cdot 5.5\cdot \tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}
                 +2\cdot 7.5\cdot \tfrac{\sqrt{231}}{2}\bigr)\\[2mm]
&= \frac12\bigl(5.5\sqrt{231}+7.5\sqrt{231}\bigr)
   = \frac12\,(13\sqrt{231})\\[2mm]
&= \boxed{ \dfrac{13\sqrt{231}}{2} } .
\end{aligned}
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4.  Final answer  

The area of the convex hexagon \(SQP_1RTP_2\) is  

\[
\boxed{\displaystyle \frac{13\sqrt{231}}{2}} .
\]

