Hence \(m=3\) indeed satisfies the required property.

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6.  Conclusion  

The only positive integer \(m>1\) for which the divisors of \(m\) can be
permuted so that every prefix sum is a perfect square is  

\[
\boxed{\,m=3\,}.
\]

