\[
\Delta = 1-4(1-p^{3}) = 4p^{3}-3 = s^{2}\qquad(s\in\mathbb Z).
\tag{2}
\]

Thus we have the Diophantine equation  

\[
s^{2}=4p^{3}-3 .
\tag{3}
\]

Because \(\Delta\) is odd, \(s\) is odd, and then  

\[
q=\frac{1+s}{2}
\tag{4}
\]

is an integer.  Moreover \(q\) is prime by the requirement of the problem.

