        \[
S=\sum_{i=1}^{2023}\frac{x_i-x_{i-1}}{x_{i+1}-x_i},
\qquad x_0=0,\;x_i>0,\;x_{i+1}\ge 2x_i\;(1\le i\le2023)
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.  Reformulation  

Put  

\[
d_i=x_i-x_{i-1}\qquad(i\ge 1),\qquad\;x_i=\sum_{k=1}^{i}d_k .
\]

The condition \(x_{i+1}\ge 2x_i\) becomes  

\[
\sum_{k=1}^{i+1}d_k\ge 2\sum_{k=1}^{i}d_k
\Longrightarrow d_{i+1}\ge\sum_{k=1}^{i}d_k=:s_i .
\tag{1}
\]

Hence  

\[
S=\sum_{i=1}^{2023}\frac{d_i}{d_{i+1}} .
\tag{2}
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.  A universal upper bound for each summand  

From (1) we have \(d_{i+1}\ge s_i\).  
Because \(s_i=s_{i-1}+d_i\) and \(s_{i-1}\ge d_{i-1}\) (again by (1) with index \(i-1\)),
\[
d_{i+1}\ge s_i = d_i+s_{i-1}\ge d_i+d_{i-1}.
\tag{3}
\]

*For \(i=1\).*  
\(d_{2}\ge s_1=d_1\), so  

\[
\frac{d_1}{d_2}\le 1 .
\tag{4}
\]

*For \(i\ge 2\).*  
From (3) and the obvious monotonicity \(d_i\ge d_{i-1}\) (which follows from (1) with
\(i-1\)),  

\[
\frac{d_i}{d_{i+1}}
\le\frac{d_i}{d_i+d_{i-1}}
\le\frac{d_i}{d_i+d_i}
=\frac12 .
\tag{5}
\]

Thus  

\[
\boxed{\displaystyle 
\frac{d_1}{d_2}\le 1,\qquad 
\frac{d_i}{d_{i+1}}\le\frac12\;(i\ge2)} .
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.  Summing the bounds  

Using (2), (4) and (5),

