--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.  A convenient notation  

Put  

\[
r_i=\frac{x_i}{x_{i-1}}\qquad (i\ge 1) .
\]

Because \(x_{i+1}\ge 2x_i\) we have  

\[
r_i\ge 2 \qquad\text{for all }i\ge 2 .
\]

For \(i\ge 1\)

\[
x_i-x_{i-1}=x_{i-1}(r_i-1),\qquad 
x_{i+1}-x_i=x_i(r_{i+1}-1)=x_{i-1}r_i(r_{i+1}-1).
\]

Hence  

\[
\frac{x_i-x_{i-1}}{x_{i+1}-x_i}= 
\frac{r_i-1}{r_i\,(r_{i+1}-1)}\qquad (i\ge 2)
\]
and for the first term  

\[
\frac{x_1-x_0}{x_2-x_1}= \frac{x_1}{x_2-x_1}= \frac{1}{r_2-1}.
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.  Transforming the expression  

Define  

\[
u_i=\frac{1}{r_i-1}\qquad (i\ge 2).
\]

Because \(r_i\ge 2\), we have  

\[
0<u_i\le 1 .
\]

Using \(r_i=1+\frac1{u_i}\) we obtain for \(i\ge 2\)

\[
\frac{r_i-1}{r_i(r_{i+1}-1)}
   =\frac{1/u_i}{\bigl(1+\frac1{u_i}\bigr)\, (1/u_{i+1})}
   =\frac{u_i u_{i+1}}{u_i+1}.
\]

Consequently the whole sum becomes  

\[
S_n:=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{x_i-x_{i-1}}{x_{i+1}-x_i}
      =u_2+\sum_{i=2}^{n}\frac{u_i u_{i+1}}{u_i+1},
      \qquad 0<u_i\le 1 .
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.  An upper bound  

For any \(0<u\le 1\),

\[
\frac{u}{u+1}\le\frac12 .
\]

Therefore for each \(i\ge 2\)

\[
\frac{u_i u_{i+1}}{u_i+1}=u_{i+1}\,\frac{u_i}{u_i+1}
        \le \frac{u_{i+1}}{2}.
\]

Using this estimate,

\[
\begin{aligned}
S_n &\le u_2+\frac12\sum_{i=3}^{n+1}u_i   \\
    &\le 1+\frac12\,(n-1)      \qquad(\text{since }u_i\le 1)\\[2mm]
    &=\frac{n+1}{2}.
\end{aligned}
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4.  Attaining the bound  

Equality in the above chain requires  

* \(u_2=1\)   \(\Longleftrightarrow\)   \(r_2=2\);
* for every \(i\ge 2\) we need \(u_i=1\) (so that \(\frac{u_i}{u_i+1}= \frac12\)).

Thus \(r_i=2\) for all \(i=2,3,\dots ,n+1\), i.e.

\[
x_{i+1}=2x_i\qquad (i=1,\dots ,n).
\]

Choosing any positive \(x_1\) and setting \(x_{i}=2^{\,i-1}x_1\) satisfies the original condition and gives

\[
\frac{x_1-0}{x_2-x_1}=1,\qquad 
\frac{x_i-x_{i-1}}{x_{i+1}-x_i}= \frac12\;(i\ge 2).
\]

Hence  

\[
S_n = 1+\frac{n-1}{2}= \frac{n+1}{2}.
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5.  The required maximal value  

For the problem \(n=2023\),

\[
\boxed{\,\displaystyle\frac{2023+1}{2}=1012\,}.
\]

Thus the maximal possible value of  

\[
\sum_{i=1}^{2023}\frac{x_i-x_{i-1}}{x_{i+1}-x_i}
\]

under the given conditions is **1012**, attained when the sequence grows exactly by a factor \(2\) at each step.

