Triggers: sumset A+B in Z/pZ, minimum size of sumset, additive combinatorics modular, |A+B| lower bound, Cauchy-Davenport inequality, subset sums mod p
Technique: Cauchy-Davenport: for non-empty A,B ⊆ Z/pZ, |A+B| ≥ min(p, |A|+|B|-1). Generalization (Kneser): for abelian groups. Plünnecke-Ruzsa: if |A+A|≤K|A|, then |nA-mA|≤K^{n+m}|A|. Use to bound sumset sizes in modular arithmetic.
