        [Turn 13 REASONING] (2337 chars)
        \[
(p+s)(r+q)=ps+qr\qquad (p,q,r,s>0)
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1.  Reducing the condition  

Expand the equality  

\[
pr+pq+sr+sq = ps+qr .
\]

Bring all terms to the left and factor:

\[
(pr-qr)+(pq-ps)+(sr+sq)=0
\]
\[
\Longrightarrow\;(p-r)(q-s)+(p-s)(r-q)=0 .
\tag{1}
\]

Hence  

\[
(p-r)(q-s)=-(p-s)(r-q).                         \tag{2}
\]

Both sides of (2) have the same sign; consequently  

\[
(p-r)(q-s)\ge 0\quad\text{and}\quad (p-s)(r-q)\le 0 .
\]

If \(p\neq s\) and \(r\neq q\) the two products in (2) have opposite
signs, which is impossible.  
Therefore at a point where the expression  

\[
F(p,q,r,s)=\frac{p}{q}+\frac{r}{p}+\frac{s}{r}+\frac{q}{s}
\]

is extremal we must have  

\[
\boxed{p=s\qquad\text{and}\qquad r=q } .
\tag{3}
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2.  One‑parameter family  

Put  

\[
p=s=t,\qquad q=r=1\;(t>0).
\]

Condition (3) is satisfied, and the original equality becomes  

\[
( t+t)(1+1)=t^{2}+1\Longrightarrow 4t=t^{2}+1 .
\]

Hence  

\[
t^{2}-4t+1=0\Longrightarrow 
t=2\pm\sqrt3 .
\tag{4}
\]

Both roots are positive; they give the same set of numbers
\((p,q,r,s)=(t,1,1,t)\).

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3.  The value of the expression  

With (3) we have  

\[
\frac{p}{q}+\frac{r}{p}+\frac{s}{r}+\frac{q}{s}
   =\frac{t}{1}+\frac{1}{t}+\frac{t}{1}+\frac{1}{t}
   =2\!\left(t+\frac1t\right).
\]

From (4) we obtain  

\[
t+\frac1t=\frac{t^{2}+1}{t}= \frac{4t}{t}=4 .
\]

Consequently  

\[
\boxed{F_{\min}=2\cdot4=8 } .
\]

--------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4.  Minimality  

For any admissible \((p,q,r,s)\) the equality (2) forces
\(p=s\) and \(r=q\) at a point where \(F\) can attain an extremum;
otherwise the two sides of (2) would have opposite signs.
Thus every extremum of \(F\) under the given condition belongs to the
family described in §2, and the only possible values of \(F\) are
\(2\bigl(t+1/t\bigr)\) with \(t\) satisfying \(t^{2}-4t+1=0\).
The unique value of this expression is \(8\).

--------------------------------------------------------------------
\[
\boxed{\displaystyle\min_{p,q,r,s>0,\;(p+s)(r+q)=ps+qr}
      \left(\frac{p}{q}+\frac{r}{p}+\frac{s}{r}+\frac{q}{s}\right)=8}
\]

