\[
(p+s)(r+q)=4pr=ps+qr=p^{2}+r^{2},
\]

which is equivalent to  

\[
\frac{p}{r}=2\pm\sqrt3 .
\]

Choosing the positive ratio \(p/r=2-\sqrt3\) (the other gives the same
values) yields exactly the numbers found above, and the value of the
required expression is \(8\).

