        [Turn 3 REASONING] (1546 chars)
        \[
a_{n+1}=2^{n}-7a_n ,\qquad n=0,1,2,\dots
\]

The homogeneous solution of the recurrence is \(C(-7)^n\).  
Seek a particular solution of the form \(A\,2^{n}\):

\[
A2^{n+1}=2^{n}-7A2^{n}\;\Longrightarrow\;2A=1-7A\;\Longrightarrow\;A=\frac19 .
\]

Hence

\[
a_n = C(-7)^n+\frac19\,2^{n}.
\]

From \(a_0\) we have \(C=a_0-\frac19\), so

\[
\boxed{a_n=\bigl(a_0-\tfrac19\bigr)(-7)^n+\frac19\,2^{n}} .
\]

---

### Monotonicity condition  

\[
\Delta_n:=a_{n+1}-a_n
      =-8\bigl(a_0-\tfrac19\bigr)(-7)^n+\frac19\,2^{n}.
\]

Write \(D=a_0-\frac19\). Then  

\[
\Delta_n = -8D(-7)^n+\frac19\,2^{n}
        =\begin{cases}
           8D\,7^{n}+\frac19\,2^{n}, & n\ \text{odd},\\[2mm]
          -8D\,7^{n}+\frac19\,2^{n}, & n\ \text{even}.
          \end{cases}
\]

The requirement \(a_{n+1}>a_n\) for every positive integer \(n\) gives

\[
\begin{aligned}
&\text{odd }n:\quad D>-\frac{1}{72}\Bigl(\frac{2}{7}\Bigr)^{n},\\[2mm]
&\text{even }n:\quad D<\frac{1}{72}\Bigl(\frac{2}{7}\Bigr)^{n}.
\end{aligned}
\]

Since \(\bigl(\frac{2}{7}\bigr)^{n}\) decreases to \(0\),

\[
-\frac{1}{72}\Bigl(\frac{2}{7}\Bigr)^{1}= -\frac{1}{252}<D\le 0 .
\]

Thus  

\[
a_0 = D+\frac19 \in\left(\frac19-\frac{1}{252},\;\frac19\right]
      =\left(\frac{3}{28},\;\frac19\right].
\]

To **minimise** \(\displaystyle\frac1{a_0}\) we need the **largest** admissible \(a_0\), namely \(a_0=\frac19\).

\[
\boxed{\displaystyle\frac1{a_0}=9 } .
\]

Indeed, with \(a_0=\frac19\) the sequence becomes \(a_n=\frac{2^{\,n}}{9}\), which satisfies \(a_{n+1}>a_n\) for all \(n\ge0\).

